-- SEC-2 legacy list: SECURITY DEFINER functions in any schema whose body names a
-- FORCE-RLS table and that are still owned by the platform BYPASSRLS owner.
-- Every one was created before Slice 09 and was not redefined by a Slice 09
-- migration (20261002*, 20261003*); the Slice 09 definers were all moved to
-- non-bypass owners (see the ownership migrations 20261003120500 and
-- 20261003150200).  The guard in phase_02_slice_09_sec2_all_schema_definer_rls.sql
-- asserts EXACT equality in both directions: a new bypass-owned definer that
-- touches a forced table fails it, and so does an entry here that has since
-- been converted or dropped.  Converting a legacy function means moving it to a
-- dedicated NOLOGIN role with matching grants and policies, and deleting its row.
create temp table sec2a_legacy(signature text primary key) on commit drop;
